1. Next.js Frontend UI Polish — Implement a modern design system with Tailwind CSS v4, dark mode aesthetics, glassmorphism, smooth micro-animations, and responsive layouts.

2. PostHog Connection — Initialize posthog-js SDK in Next.js to track user logins, project creation, and Hackatime linking events.

3. Lapse Reviewing Connection — Integrate Lapse API (api.lapse.hackclub.com) to stream timelapse video recordings for submission reviews.

4. Reviewer Database & PII Scoping — Set up reviewer database tables (ReviewerNote, ReviewerChecklist) and enforce strict PII redaction (scopeUserData()).

5. Fraud Review Connection — Connect Joe Fraud Review API (joe.fraud.hackclub.com) for fraud flagging, match highlighting, and review verdicts.

6. Pentesting & Security Hardening — Audit OAuth state/redirect parameter safety, enforce cookie flags (HttpOnly/SameSite), 
rate limit endpoints, and verify role RBAC guards.

7. OpenAPI Client Generation — Auto-generate typed OpenAPI fetch clients (generate:api) for Next.js endpoints to maintain strict backend-frontend contract safety.

8. Slack DM & Event Notifications — Connect internal Slack service to trigger automated DM notifications on project approval, rejection, and fraud flags.

9. Airtable Sync Pipeline — Set up background Airtable sync routines for participant records, project metrics, and shop purchases.

10. Production Deployment & Monitoring — Configure Docker container builds, health check monitoring (/health), and environment variable configs for live deployment.
